Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:07:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] perf: city programs specialised by material for Adreno
 GPUs

city.wgsl's fragment program is one branch per material plus the debug
views: Turnip's compiler turns it into ~21 000 instructions at the
register limit, and the city pass took ~370 ms a frame on an Adreno 740.
Each (pipeline, material, sample count) gets its own pipeline built from
the same text with the material fixed and the debug views left out
(2 500 - 5 500 instructions), on worker threads; the shared pipeline
draws until it is ready. The ones drawn are listed in city-programs.txt
in the user folder and built as the next game starts. The current city
pipeline is kept per thread, as the city pass is recorded on two.
MCLA_CITY_SPEC=0: the shared pipelines only.
